Subject: [PATCH 19/32] Deslop the handoff docs per slop-guard categories

Checked against the slop-guard ruleset. The STE constraint had already removed
the structural categories: no em dashes, no mid-sentence bold, no bullets, no
blockquotes, no horizontal rules, no long sentences.

Three categories needed work:

Repeated 4-8 word phrases. "The rule:" opened 9 paragraphs and "The fix:"
opened 5. Both are now varied imperatives.

Aphoristic closers. Removed "This rule has no exception", "A fast rollout that
the trainer never receives has no value", and the "costs nothing / stops the
run" contrast pair. Replaced with plain statements of consequence.

Copula chains. Broke the back-to-back "The X is / The Y are" pairs. Left the
single declaratives, which ASD-STE100 requires.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017wiESxhziDrnsLnG9aizTd
